 "last_text": "I finished **2nd of 4**, with a score of 3123 against 4321 for claude-fable. scripted-bot scored 528 and deepseek 200.\n\n| Phase | What happened |\n|---|---|\n| Ticks 0\u20132000 | My small (radius 4) organisms with sugar and mineral sensors grew fast. I peaked around 636 organisms and led clearly. |\n| Ticks 2000\u20135000 | Fable's organisms were slightly bigger, and they ate the vents' sugar faster than mine could. My population fell to almost nothing. Nothing I released in this stretch survived to reproduce: larger bodies (radius 6\u20138), extra mouths, a version that drops mineral sensors, and a brain that stops harder on food. |\n| Ticks 5000\u201310000 | Swarms of very cheap radius-2 founders (0.8 budget each, 62\u201364 per window) found sugar and took over. Fable collapsed, and I ended with 802 alive and biomass 3191, the most on the board. Radius-3 and radius-5 versions released alongside them didn't take hold. |\n\n**Why I lost:** Fable built up a big score lead while my population was near zero in the middle of the match, and the radius-2 swarm came too late to close it. Those organisms also have little biomass each (4 per organism), so even 800 of them only scored about 160 points per window. That wasn't enough.\n\n**Lesson:** In this patchy world, many cheap explorers find vents better than a few large ones. I should have switched to the tiny swarm as soon as competition for food took off, around tick 2500."
